1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,407
Pneumono, ultra, microscopic, silico, volcano, coni, osis.

2
00:00:04,407 --> 00:00:05,651
Forty five letters.

3
00:00:05,651 --> 00:00:07,455
A ward round in the morning.

4
00:00:07,455 --> 00:00:09,880
And a word you have never seen before.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:15,330
Can you say it out loud?

6
00:00:15,330 --> 00:00:16,938
Can you spell it on a chart?

7
00:00:16,938 --> 00:00:19,820
And when someone asks what it means, will you know?

8
00:00:20,420 --> 00:00:20,935
Breathe.

9
00:00:20,935 --> 00:00:24,151
Long words are just small parts, joined together.

10
00:00:24,151 --> 00:00:25,180
MedLex has you.

11
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:30,022
It starts with a puzzle.

12
00:00:30,022 --> 00:00:34,500
Tap peri, card and itis, and pericarditis explains itself.

13
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:36,625
Every answer shows you why.

14
00:00:36,625 --> 00:00:38,219
Gastr means stomach.

15
00:00:38,219 --> 00:00:40,800
Add itis, and you have gastritis.

16
00:00:50,283 --> 00:00:55,242
Your day is ten minutes and ten words, mixing new terms with smart reviews.

17
00:00:55,242 --> 00:00:57,357
Match each part to its meaning.

18
00:00:57,357 --> 00:01:00,663
Then flip it around, and build the word yourself.

19
00:01:12,367 --> 00:01:17,284
Every term in the library is taken apart, explained in plain words, and spoken aloud.

20
00:01:17,284 --> 00:01:22,027
Sixty six prefixes, sixty roots and a hundred suffixes, each with its own studio.

21
00:01:34,450 --> 00:01:37,206
Illustrated guides decode a term in five steps.

22
00:01:37,206 --> 00:01:43,070
Each body system lives on one beautiful canvas, with a hundred terms and outcomes you can tick off.

23
00:01:56,533 --> 00:01:59,575
Root cards give you a picture and a hook.

24
00:01:59,575 --> 00:02:00,910
Card means heart.

25
00:02:00,910 --> 00:02:02,172
Hemi means half.

26
00:02:02,172 --> 00:02:05,733
A quick check after every card proves it stuck.

27
00:02:18,617 --> 00:02:24,755
Travel nine eras of medical language, from ancient Egypt to Vesalius.

28
00:02:24,755 --> 00:02:29,737
And watch your mastery grow, one body system at a time.

29
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:42,600
Fourteen hundred and eighty terms.

30
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:43,776
Twenty six modules.

31
00:02:43,776 --> 00:02:45,540
Fifty six illustrated guides.

32
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:51,687
MedLex is free to start.

33
00:02:51,687 --> 00:02:55,011
The full app comes with the Crown Pass, with seven days free.

34
00:02:55,011 --> 00:02:56,620
Decode your first word today.
